Well, last night, I finally did it.  After months of playing, I won.  Legit,
even.  Oh, what a feeling... :-)

Now, for the reason for the posting:  First, true to what has been said 
earlier, patch 10 makes it so that initially stoning the wizard won't keep
him down permanently.  I know, since I whapped him with a cockatrice corpse
and ran upstairs.  He showed up again a few levels later...

Second, once in a while I got a message along the lines of "Double trouble",
and all of a sudden there were two wizards (and, I think, three, at one
point).  Strangely enough, at only one wizard showed up as an @;  the other
showed up as an x.  When I id'd the character, it said something like "a
xan or other mythological beast (Wizard of Yendor)".  Strange.  Anyway, is
the doubling of the Wizard new?  I don't recall ever seeing it before, or
even reading about it...

Notes and ramblings...

The wizard cursed my ring of conflict, so I couldn't take it off.  He also
cursed my potions of holy water, so I couldn't uncursed it.  (The way nethack
treats multiple items is both a bug and a feature, so I won't complain about
it...)  However, it's awfully annoying to get to the end level, go into the
room of Liches, have them start beating on each other, and "The lich isn't
affected by the cold" followed by 5 seconds of pulsing graphics characters...
There should be a way to shorten how long the "not effected" thing goes on
for.  It took me 15 minutes just to move across the room, kick open the
secret door (thank the gods it was where I figured it'd be) and get out.

Almost blew it at the end, too.  Had a cockatrice corpse and fell into a
pit.  Thank the gods again for the amulet of life saving... (whew!).  I
would have died literally 10 steps from my altar.... 

Well, so much for barbarian.  Wonder which way I'll make it next?  (Hopefully
it won't take another 6 months :)

